    tier: 'Top IIMs and a handful of elite institutes',
    numbers: 'IIM Calcutta 2026: average Rs 36 LPA, median Rs 35 LPA, 458 students, 542 offers, 202 recruiters. IIM Bangalore 2024-26: average Rs 35.35 LPA.',
    doors: 'Consulting, finance, product, general management, FMCG brand roles. Almost every lane above is open on day one.',
  },
  {
    tier: 'Lower IIMs and strong private institutes',
    numbers: 'IIM Lucknow 2024-26: average Rs 33.2 LPA, median Rs 32.9 LPA. IIM Indore average slipped from Rs 29.57 LPA (2023-25) to about Rs 27.3 LPA with a Rs 25 LPA median (2024-26). XLRI 2024-26: average Rs 31.4 LPA, median Rs 29 LPA. Newer IIMs sit lower: Visakhapatnam Rs 15.7 LPA average, Sirmaur Rs 13.3 LPA (2024-25).',
    doors: 'Consulting at second-tier firms, BFSI, analytics, FMCG sales and marketing, operations. Spread between average and median is wider, so ask for the median.',
  },
  {
    tier: 'Tier-2 private institutes',
    numbers: 'Careers360 puts the average at Rs 10-20 LPA for the tier. One undated listing shows fees of Rs 14-24 lakh against averages of Rs 9-19 LPA, so fee is often 1.3 to 1.9 times a year of average pay (table below).',
    doors: 'BFSI relationship and credit roles, sales and business development, HR generalist, operations, analyst roles at services firms. Consulting and product open later.',
  },
  {
    tier: 'Tier-3 and low-cutoff colleges',
    numbers: 'In NIRF 2022 data (2020-21 batch), 29 of the top 100 management institutes reported a median salary below Rs 6 lakh, and those 29 placed only 67.7% of graduates (4,199 of 6,202). The data is old and pandemic-affected, so treat it as a warning, not a forecast.',
    doors: 'Sales, tele-banking, insurance, collections, and back-office roles. Real progress comes from a skill layer and job switches, not from the degree.',
