  <h2 id="market-now">What hiring data says right now</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consulting leads at the top.</strong> It was the largest hiring domain at IIM Mumbai in 2026 and took 36% to 45% of offers at the institutes in the table above.</li>
    <li><strong>BFSI is mixed.</strong> IIM Mumbai reported BFSI hiring up 33%, yet Naukri JobSpeak showed banking-sector hiring down 15% year on year in May 2026 and 12% in June. Top-institute finance roles and volume banking roles are behaving differently.</li>
    <li><strong>Frontline roles are growing.</strong> Naukri's May 2026 data showed fresher relationship manager roles up 75%, loan officer roles up 62% and retail sales up 50%. They are not glamorous, but they are where the volume is.</li>
    <li><strong>AI and machine-learning hiring is up</strong> 22% year on year in May 2026 and 25% in June, while overall fresher hiring grew 7% to 8%. That favours MBAs who can pair analytics with a business function.</li>
    <li><strong>Pay at the top is flat to slightly lower.</strong> IIM Indore's average fell from Rs 29.57 lakh (2023-25) to about Rs 27.3 lakh (2024-26), about 8%, although the batch mix may differ. XLRI's median held at Rs 29 LPA while its highest domestic offer dropped from Rs 75 lakh to Rs 59 lakh.</li>
    <li><strong>Employers still want MBAs, with a catch.</strong> GMAC's 2026 recruiter survey (621 recruiters, 39 countries) found 39% planning to expand MBA hiring, while one in three had already replaced some entry-level roles with AI.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Read these as direction, not destiny. Your lane matters more than the average.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai-and-mba-jobs">AI and the entry-level MBA job</h2>

  <p>
    The honest risk is at the bottom of the ladder. GMAC's 2026 Corporate Recruiters Survey found that one-third of employers have already replaced at least some
    entry-level roles with AI, most often in technology (40%) and manufacturing (36%). Recruiters ranked communication (64%), problem-solving
    (62%) and data analysis (59%) as the skills they value now, and AI tool proficiency (53%) as the top skill for the next five years.
  </p>

  <p>
    First-draft research, template financial models, and routine reports are the kind of tasks most exposed, so an
    entry-level seat built only on them is the risky one.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Start now</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Use AI for research drafts, then check every number yourself.</li>
        <li>Rebuild one part of your current or project work with AI and record the time saved.</li>
        <li>Learn SQL and spreadsheets well enough to spot a wrong AI answer.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Build toward</div>
