  <h2 id="money-check">The money check before you sign a fee form</h2>

  <p>
    Use a strict planning heuristic: if the full education budget is Rs 10 lakh, about Rs 1 lakh is a
    conservative starting benchmark for college fees, and spending above roughly 20% is a serious caution point that needs course
    specific evidence. This is a heuristic, not a law. Most MBA fees will cross it, so the burden of proof
    rises: verified median placement, your lane's recruiters on campus, and a payback plan that survives a
    weak first year.
  </p>

  <p>
    A fee of Rs 20 lakh would only pass the 20% caution line for a family with a Rs 1 crore education budget, so
    most MBA plans rest on a loan. That makes the fee-to-pay ratio the number to compute first.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
